my name is Mandy Eccleston I graduated  from Hillsdale in 2012 my running career  started when I was 12 years old I first  started running when I saw my sister  compete the year before me and I really  wanted to do it as well I had a lot of  fun going to her meets and watching and  knew it was something I wanted to  continue I just wasn't sure where I  wanted to go right away  Hillsdale stood out to me a lot because  of the coaches it was bill Lumbergh and  Sarah Hinkley at the time and they were  just so welcoming and so excited about  me as an athlete that it really made me  want to come and be a part of their team  I met my husband on the team my best  friends are on the team from there and  my senior year just everything really  came together it was kind of a perfect  year in terms of running I won three  national championships that year to an  indoor 'none and outdoor and that's  something I never had even imagined you  know coming into Hillsdale I had just  thought I want to make Nationals one  time and that would be you know such a  huge goal and then to be able to win  three titles is really exciting and then  I was lucky enough after graduating I  had some eligibility left from getting  hurt  so I ran at the University of Michigan  for a year and then since then I have  been continuing running professionally  you know I would say a dream come true  but it wasn't even a dream when I was  younger because I didn't realize that  professional running was a thing or that  it could you know become an actual  career  [Music]  at Hillsdale the team was a huge part of  my life not only were those my friends  and my roommates those are just the  people who kept you accountable it's  really cool to be a part of a team  I know people talk about running as an  individual sport but it's really not  there's no way you could do everything  by yourself I'm very honored to enter  the Hillsdale Hall of Fame so I really  appreciate being recognized by Hillsdale  and that you know they appreciate what  I've been able to do for them as an  athlete it was definitely one of my  favorite things to wear that uniform and  race for those four years so I'm really  excited to be a part of it and you know  to be there I guess forever in history  as a part of that so I appreciate this a  lot  [Music]
 

